</SPT></SPT><SPT><TTL>EXCAVATION VERIFICATION</TTL><BRK/>
<NTE><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/>
<NPR>NOTE:  This Blasting Section presumes that the excavation(s) will fully achieve 
the required vertical and lateral limits.  This paragraph references the location 
of the verification procedures by its section in the specifications.</NPR><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/></NTE>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Conduct the verification of the completed excavation, as specified in Section [EXCAVATION], Paragraph [SURVEYS].</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
<SPT><TTL>SUBMERGED MATERIAL DISPOSAL</TTL><BRK/>
<NTE><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/>
<NPR>NOTE:  The Guide Spec presumes that material disposal will properly place any 
onsite material disposal. This paragraph references the location of the material 
disposal procedures by its section in the specifications.</NPR><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/></NTE>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Transport and place all dredged, displaced, or excavated materials within the limits of the disposal zones below 
the specified elevations, as specified in Section [DISPOSAL].</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
</PRT>    <END/><BRK/></SEC>